 "limits": "Evidence: KuaiRand-Pure (27,285 anonymised Kuaishou users chosen by the KuaiRand authors (China, 2022); interactions only with the 7,583 videos of the random-exposure pool); Kuaishou short-video app, single-column featured feed (tab 1); 2022-04-08 to 2022-05-08. The model gives the distribution of log1p(watch seconds) of one feed exposure given whether it was consumed, the item's duration and the affinity/popularity inputs. The simulator may draw watch time for autoplay short-video exposures with durations of 6 s to 20 min. It may NOT infer: watch time for long-form video, live streams, articles or audio; durations outside the data range; effects of interventions on watch time (all associations are observational); other populations or periods. Quantiles outside the 2%-98% levels are extrapolated linearly over one quantile gap, so extreme replays (play ratios above about 4) are not reproduced; the skip branch (consumed = 0) is dominated by the platform's autoplay, so it describes how long an autoplaying video runs before the individual swipes away.",
